            "review_title": "Review at Pyramids Restaurant Halal",
            "review_text": "Kevin M\n6 contributions\n0\nDisappointing food ...\nAug 2025 • Solo\nI ate lunch at the Pyramids – my first time there. The restaurant is festooned with Egyptian motifs – the Pyramids, gods and goddesses, pharaohs and Mo Salah. Very eye-catching. There is a shop upstairs selling Egyptian souvenirs – papyri, statues, t-shirts.\nMany items on the menu looked expensive to me, so I ordered humus, babaganoush, a lamb kofta and Egyptian bread. The two friendly young waitresses gave me a free glass of water and free pickled vegetables with garlic sauce. When I finished the pickles, the waitress gave me some more.\nI had to wait 20 minutes for the food to arrive. The lamb and the hummus were disappointingly bland, but the babaganoush was tasty. I half-finished the hummus and babaganoush and took home the remainder.\nFinally, they gave me a free cup of mint tea.\nThe bill was 250,000 VND, which included 8% tax. I consider this slightly expensive. \nPyramids compares unfavourably, both price-wise and food-wise, with Al Sham Syrian Restaurant and Cleopatra. \nI am not sure that I will eat here again.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 31, 2025",
